|\mathbf{d_1} \times \mathbf{d_2}| = \sqrt{(-4)^2 + 3^2 + 6^2} = \sqrt{16 + 9 + 36} = \sqrt{61}
\] The dot product \((\mathbf{r_0}_2 - \mathbf{r_0}_1) \cdot (\mathbf{d_1} \times \mathbf{d_2})\) is calculated as: \[
(\mathbf{r_0}_2 - \mathbf{r_0}_1) = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 0 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -1 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 1 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}
